## Design Rationale

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| 9-stage pipeline vs. monolith | Isolates failure points; each stage can be tested, replaced, or scaled independently |
| Chunking configurable via `.env` not hardcoded | Research flaw #4: poor chunking silently propagates errors; making it configurable prevents user surprise |
| Mandatory user review gate (Stage 4) | Research flaw #3: "evaluation-induced optimization"; human in the loop prevents metric gaming |
| Two API configs in `.env` | Separation of concerns: question-generation AI vs. target RAG endpoint; different providers, different auth patterns |
| Metric cross-validation with ≥2 frameworks | Research flaw #1 + #2: single-framework metrics are vulnerable to gaming and coverage gaps |
| Contamination check opt-in (`EVAL_CONTAMINATION_CHECK`) | Research flaw #5: data contamination is user-dependent; opt-in avoids performance hit for trusted users |
| Periodic re-evaluation reminder | Research flaw #7: evaluation paradigms evolve; 3-month cadence keeps system current without constant monitoring |

